WEBVTT

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.520
Toh! Toh! Toh!

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:09.390
Keep going!

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:12.460
The weather's turned bad suddenly!

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:15.030
We need to get somewhere safe now!

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.540
I can't even see anymore!

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:26.430
Ryu, what are you doing?

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:27.820
Stay in formation!

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.170
You don't think he's spotted something?

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.720
Ryu was never cut out to pull a sled!

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.670
He's a hunting dog!

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.000
Ryu!

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.700
Where are you going?

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:40.950
Go straight!

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:47.420
Henke says he see something!

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:48.360
Stop the sled!

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:50.940
The others aren't with us!

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:56.760
Sugimoto!

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:01.120
Was that a gunshot?

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.000
Did we get separated?

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.640
Where did the gunshot come from?

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:08.420
I think that way!

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:18.360
Did you hear something?

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:20.290
What?

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:25.330
It's no good!

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:26.730
We need to find shelter somewhere!

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:31.140
We need to at least... find a 
place to get away from the wind.

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:41.480
What? We came all the way to the coast?

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:44.310
That's not good.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:46.000
We need to do something...

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:47.640
Or we're dead!

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:18.840
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:29.330
<b>Episode Thirty-One
Meko Oyasi</b>

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:27.560
Damn it!

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:33.480
The ground... is frozen solid.

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:36.110
We'll just need to do something.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:37.860
Destroy the sled.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:44.530
Tsukishima, we're in real danger here!

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:48.540
Let's go!

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:51.200
We'll head to that building 
they said they saw!

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:58.850
Yes!

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:03.050
Hey, what are you doing?

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:07.680
A sled's worth of firewood 
won't last long at all.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:11.680
But if we bury it, 
it'll burn slowly in the Earth.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:16.060
If we lie down on it, we can 
stay warm a little longer.

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:19.980
That's right Tanigaki, you're a Matagi.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:21.930
But the hole's not deep enough.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:24.100
It won't serve to do much 
but keep off the wind.

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:26.370
You guys! Come here!

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:33.000
It's a Karafuto dog blanket.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:37.880
Will the dogs be okay?

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:42.380
They're fine. They handle the cold well.

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:45.420
The question is, how long will we last?

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:48.770
The sun will set soon.

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:53.470
There're cows here, Tsukishima!

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:55.450
Someone lives here!

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:58.360
Let's worry about finding the 
person who lives here later.

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:00.570
For now, let's start a fire.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.220
What about the others?

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:04.300
With Tanigaki with them,

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:07.690
they should be okay for a while...

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:12.790
Here.

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:15.130
There's not much,

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:18.730
but eating makes a big difference when 
trying to maintain your temperature.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.760
Open your mouth. Here.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:28.830
I feel like I've had this before.

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:30.700
That's impossible.

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:33.370
This is a secret recipe for mochi 
from the place where I grew up,

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.420
and I've also adjusted the flavoring a little.

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:38.840
Yeah?

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:41.760
That's strange.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:45.930
I remember eating this...

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:52.620
Was that a gunshot?

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.450
Or thunder?

00:05:54.800 --> 00:06:01.800
In the middle of a blizzard, you can be 
shouting at each other and still get lost.

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:05.470
You can't trust your sense of direction here.

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:12.220
What's wrong?

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:14.640
What are you doing there?

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:16.650
The man who lives here?

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:20.000
Our friends are lost nearby!

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.070
Come with me!

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:27.590
This way! Hurry!!

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:39.270
This way! Hurry!!

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:50.650
We haven't used this for a while. 
The inside is sooty, so wipe it clean.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:53.080
What's this?

00:06:55.820 --> 00:07:00.430
Being in this cold hole 
reminds me of the trenches.

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:06.920
Don't go to sleep, Sugimoto.

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:08.920
You'll die.

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:10.720
Yeah.

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:14.990
It's cold.

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:22.670
It's cold, Toraji.

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:25.670
I want to go home, Saichi.

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:32.700
I want to go home.

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:00.590
...imoto.

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:05.210
Asirpa-san...

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:07.550
Sugimoto.

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:18.290
Light...

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:22.920
Hey, can you see that light?

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:24.410
Is it the moon?

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:28.860
No. It's been exactly two months 
since we attacked Abashiri.

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:31.410
The moon shouldn't be that big.

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:34.120
It's shining...

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:35.860
That's not moonlight.

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:37.180
That's...

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:39.590
A lighthouse!

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:42.370
Lieutenant...

00:08:42.990 --> 00:08:44.500
Lieutenant Koito.

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:47.130
Please don't wander around 
in front of the lens.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:49.410
You're blocking the light.

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:53.630
<b>enarC</b>

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:11.960
This "sushka" goes very well with tea.

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:14.880
I'd love to have Lieutenant Tsurumi try it.

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:19.970
This way.

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:23.720
The warmest spot in this 
room is above the pechka.

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:26.230
The Russians sleep there, too.

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:29.640
They look like bugs.

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:35.760
You got lucky.

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:40.760
This lighthouse hasn't been used 
since the Russo-Japanese War.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:45.880
And if these people weren't here, 
you'd be frozen solid right now.

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:48.100
Thank you!

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:01.370
Sorry for burning your sled.

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:04.950
You're done?

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:07.180
Wow, and you just made this 
with what was lying around!

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:08.550
This is amazing!

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:10.380
Amazing, Henke!

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:13.210
Okay, now we can go!

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:18.130
Looking back, I think the reason 
Ryu broke off from the line

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:21.850
was that he was trying to 
stay with the other sled.

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:24.430
Sorry for doubting you.

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:27.230
You're a great dog.

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:30.100
You can be a great sled dog, too!

00:10:32.030 --> 00:10:35.350
Tsukishima, the hammer froze to my hand!

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:39.780
That's what'll happen if you touch 
metal bare-handed at this temperature.

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:42.740
If you try to rip it off, 
it'll tear away the skin on your hand.

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:47.510
Somebody piss on it to melt it.

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.750
I can do it.

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:58.120
Show me your hand.

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:12.480
What's this soup?

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:13.560
It's bright red!

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:16.860
This is borscht.

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:19.170
The red comes from a vegetable called a "beet."

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:22.340
What's Russian for "yummy"?

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:24.070
Vkusno.

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:25.610
Vkusno!

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:26.660
Vkusno.

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:28.080
Vkusno!

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:35.840
It's normally just the two of them, 
so they're happy to have the company.

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:38.380
You don't have any family?

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:42.310
Is that your daughter in that photo?

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:46.810
What's wrong?

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:58.610
The three of us lived here in peace, 
watching the lighthouse, since before the war.

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:05.120
But one day, a Russian deserter 
appeared and lived here for a while.

00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:10.760
He took away their only daughter.

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:15.630
They searched for her, but didn't find her.

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:20.340
The military and government did nothing.

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:25.220
When the Japanese landed in Karafuto,

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:29.810
the Russian government had given them 
explosives to destroy the lighthouse,

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:31.570
to keep it from being used by the Japanese.

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:34.610
But when the Japanese army came,

00:12:34.610 --> 00:12:36.910
they were so angry at the Russian 
government that they handed it over.

00:12:38.330 --> 00:12:41.500
Later, another lighthouse 
was built to the north,

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:43.030
and there was no need for this place.

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:49.660
But the two of them stay here and 
wait for their daughter's return.

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:03.170
So because of what happened with 
their daughter, the lighthouse remained,

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:06.180
and our lives were saved, huh?

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:12.100
Can I take a photo of your daughter?

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:17.100
What's her name?

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:19.670
Svetlana.

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:25.010
Thank you for everything!

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:26.510
Please!

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:32.640
Please find our daughter! Find Svetlana!

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:34.680
Hey, Sugimoto.

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:36.610
I know.

00:13:36.610 --> 00:13:39.750
It won't take too much time 
to ask around on our travels.

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:43.260
I can't leave without 
doing nothing in return.

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:48.010
Ma'am, please put this photo 
of mine in that empty frame.

00:13:48.650 --> 00:13:54.970
If this Ainu girls comes by, 
tell her that Saichi Sugimoto is alive.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:58.020
Okay, go!

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:03.510
Toh! Toh! Toh!

00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:20.040
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:21.420
Asirpa.

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:22.540
Asirpa.

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:24.480
Never seen her.

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:25.840
Okay...

00:14:26.450 --> 00:14:27.400
What about her?

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:29.320
Never seen her.

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:36.650
<i>Sugimoto's group was staying at a 
Karafuto Ainu village near Niitoi.</i>

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:37.500
<b>Border</b>

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:37.500
<b>Sugimoto's Position</b>

00:14:37.840 --> 00:14:41.490
<i>There were only 140 kilometers 
left until the border.</i>

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:44.990
Cikapasi, listen!

00:14:44.990 --> 00:14:47.690
There was a meko oyasi sighted 
in this village a while ago!

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:49.910
What's that? Is it scary?

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:54.420
A cat monster found in the 
legends of the Karafuto Ainu!

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:58.110
Someone dropped all their stuff 
on the beach and went to work,

00:14:58.110 --> 00:15:00.180
and a meko oyasi appeared!

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:05.590
They fled on their ship, and a bunch 
of the things appeared on the beach!

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:08.470
They were staring at the ship and howling!

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:14.580
A big cat the size of a dog, 
with red and white spots!

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:17.430
A large mountain cat.

00:15:19.240 --> 00:15:21.310
Sure it's not Ogata Hyakunosuke?

00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:23.140
Why Ogata?

00:15:26.870 --> 00:15:29.390
The child of a mountain cat
 is a mountain cat.

00:15:30.730 --> 00:15:31.940
What's that mean?

00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:35.830
"Mountain cat" is slang for geisha.

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:40.080
It's a dumb joke the men in 
the division used to tell.

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:42.390
That really is dumb.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:46.460
Given his personality, 
a lot of men didn't like him.

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:48.820
I hate him.

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:55.550
"Mountain cat" also means 
to con or deceive somebody.

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:58.370
Sounds perfect for him, right?

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:01.480
Or am I wrong, Sugimoto?

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:06.440
What happened to the meko oyasi?

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:12.640
They came back later, and there were lots 
of paw prints, and all their stuff was gone.

00:16:12.640 --> 00:16:15.430
Their clothes, their shoes, 
their bags, all of it!

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:17.900
They ate it?

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:19.370
Maybe.

00:16:20.850 --> 00:16:22.290
Even their tobacco cases?

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:27.130
No. Those stink. They wouldn't 
eat them, I don't think.

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:29.250
Scary.

00:16:30.040 --> 00:16:33.000
If there's any lesson to be 
had in that bizarre story,

00:16:33.850 --> 00:16:36.860
it's that it's best to kill thieving cats.

00:16:52.850 --> 00:16:54.110
What are these prints?

00:16:55.190 --> 00:16:57.350
They're like a meko, but too big!

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.120
What's a meko?

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:01.490
A cat.

00:17:02.180 --> 00:17:04.770
It means "those that die in cold."

00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:07.890
You couldn't give them a cuter name?

00:17:07.890 --> 00:17:10.250
Those are the prints of a mountain cat.

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:12.920
Is this a meko oyasi?

00:17:13.530 --> 00:17:18.030
So this was the cat monster 
Aca once told me about!

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:24.670
Their shoes, their clothes, their bags,
 their ropes, it was all gone.

00:17:24.670 --> 00:17:27.510
Maybe the meko oyasi ate it!

00:17:27.510 --> 00:17:29.020
Even their tobacco cases?

00:17:29.260 --> 00:17:32.930
Yeah. I hunted one with Wilk, just once.

00:17:33.470 --> 00:17:35.780
We made a ton off its pelt.

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:36.780
What did it taste like?

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:40.140
Not good. Very gamy.

00:17:40.140 --> 00:17:43.170
Your father seemed to hate it.

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:48.920
I see... so the cat monster 
doesn't taste good, huh?

00:17:50.070 --> 00:17:52.540
It's the first time I've ever 
heard that story about Aca!

00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:56.800
Do you want to know more?

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:03.850
There's a woman named Sofia 
who knew the old Wilk well.

00:18:04.570 --> 00:18:09.790
She was brave and well-educated. Our leader.

00:18:13.910 --> 00:18:16.030
And very beautiful.

00:18:16.520 --> 00:18:19.870
We both looked up to her.

00:18:21.260 --> 00:18:22.240
Aca did...

00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:24.700
I didn't know there was anyone like that.

00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:26.890
I want to meet her.

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:29.480
Where is she?

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:32.780
Aleksandrovsk-Sakhalinsky...

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:35.470
Ako.

00:18:36.660 --> 00:18:41.400
<i>Aleksandrovsk-Sakhalinsky, 
also known as "Ako,"</i>

00:18:40.150 --> 00:18:44.890
<b>Ako</b>

00:18:40.150 --> 00:18:44.890
<b>Border</b>

00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:45.360
<i>is a major city in the 
Russian part of Karafuto.</i>

00:18:45.820 --> 00:18:47.930
<i>Since 1858,</i>

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:53.900
<i>Karafuto was used as a place 
to exile criminals from the mainland.</i>

00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:58.190
<i>And Ako was the place they first landed.</i>

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:06.910
<i>Aleksandrovsk-Sakhalinsky Prison holds, at the
 height of its use, about 1,700 prisoners.</i>

00:18:59.670 --> 00:19:06.910
<b>Aleksandrovsk-Sakhalinsky Prison
 (Ako Prison)</b>

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:11.670
<i>Male prisoners had half their hair cut,</i>

00:19:12.470 --> 00:19:15.460
<i>and were primarily forced to do hard 
labor in mining and construction.</i>

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:21.330
<i>Those who escaped would be 
brought back and whipped.</i>

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:24.600
<i>Those who tried more than once 
would be tied to a wheelbarrow</i>

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:26.720
<i>that would stay with them 
even as they ate and slept.</i>

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:28.430
Xopoшo!

00:19:29.430 --> 00:19:32.800
They're kept in Ako Prison.

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:37.320
There's no evidence,
 so they can't be executed.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:39.920
But they're kept locked away in secret.

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:44.520
She was the one behind our plot 
to assassinate the emperor.

00:19:45.340 --> 00:19:52.020
You were too soft. I went to sleep!

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:55.930
Sofia Goldenhand.

00:19:56.450 --> 00:20:00.740
She would commit crimes 
to fund our activities.

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:05.240
So she was given the name 
"Golden Hand" at court.

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:07.530
A woman?

00:20:07.530 --> 00:20:09.520
Your boss was a woman?

00:20:09.840 --> 00:20:10.750
Yeah.

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:14.770
She would know things 
about Wilk that I don't know.

00:20:18.510 --> 00:20:20.090
Ako Prison...

00:20:20.090 --> 00:20:21.170
If we go there...

00:20:35.090 --> 00:20:36.000
Ogata,

00:20:37.810 --> 00:20:38.920
we're heading to Ako!

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:46.080
Was something there?

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:47.650
Let's go.

00:22:38.930 --> 00:22:44.610
A female prisoner can 
leave if she gets married.

00:22:45.110 --> 00:22:51.450
You're young. 
Find a man and get married, Svetlana.

00:22:55.370 --> 00:22:58.830
You have a letter, Sofia Goldenhand.

00:23:18.470 --> 00:23:20.600
Yulbars!

00:23:22.770 --> 00:23:25.770
You've come back, huh, kid?

